<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">398 BCE – 380 BCE · capital Mendes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Delta dynasty from Mendes that kept Egypt independent of Persia in the early 4th century BCE through Greek alliances.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 399 to 398 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-i">Nepherites I</a>, a general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendes">Mendes</a> in the central Delta, overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyrtaeus">Amyrtaeus</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-eighth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-eighth Dynasty of Egypt</a> and founded a new line. He sent grain and ships to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a>, then at war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, and built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a> and Mendes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty's strongest king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakor">Hakor</a> (Achoris), ruled for about thirteen years. He allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evagoras-i">Evagoras</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a>, hired Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> under the Athenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chabrias">Chabrias</a> and repelled a Persian attack around 385 to 383 BCE. He was an active builder, restoring temples across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Rivalry between family branches weakened the throne, with short reigns by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psammuthes">Psammuthes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-ii">Nepherites II</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 380 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-i">Nectanebo I</a>, a general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebennytos">Sebennytos</a>, deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-ii">Nepherites II</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thirtieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Thirtieth Dynasty of Egypt</a>. The remains of a royal tomb at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendes">Mendes</a>, probably that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-i">Nepherites I</a>, have been excavated, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakor">Hakor's</a> building works were often reinscribed by his successors.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/twenty-ninth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="231"><figcaption>Image: Enyavar (German original), Redx360 (English translation) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Near_East_400BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>398 BCE – 380 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mendes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nepherites I, Hakor</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Twenty-ninth Dynasty, Mendesian Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-389&amp;focus=twenty-ninth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5495 1049 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5815 1305L5796 1305M5815 1305L5808 1305"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5796 1305h0M5808 1305h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5815 1305h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5815 1305h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mendes. <a href="/atlas?year=-389&amp;focus=twenty-ninth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
